# Vanessa Security Warning Handling Policy

> RULES — mandatory requirements for interpreting launch blocks via `Предупреждение безопасности`.

## Purpose

When launching the external processing `bddRunner.epf` or its plugins, the 1C platform may display a modal `Предупреждение безопасности`. This is a separate class of blockers that cannot be reliably diagnosed only via the event log or only via window titles.

## MUST

| Requirement | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| ЖР как триггер | If the ЖР contains an entry about `Предупреждение безопасности`, the agent MUST treat it as a trigger for visual verification |
| Visual verification is mandatory | After this signal, the agent MUST rely on a real screen: noVNC or a screenshot |
| Do not rely on X11 heuristics | Conclusions cannot be made solely from `wmctrl`/`xwininfo`/window titles |
| Trust-flow only for the first run | The first launch after changing the EPF is not considered a valid test run |

The detailed procedure is described in the diagnostics and GUI skills.

